{"id":"u-22c9c5da-c32e-4e94-92ce-b256769c9bef","src":"community","title":"Bullmastiff X5","author":"Umar K.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/yZjo5L-bullmastiff-x5","desc":"Bullmastiff X5 is a 5-day powerbuilding program designed to maximize strength, muscle mass, and work capacity through a combination of heavy compound lifting and targeted hypertrophy training. The program retains the progressive overload philosophy of Bullmastiff while distributing volume across five training days, allowing lifters to recover effectively while increasing training frequency.\nThe primary goals are:\nIncrease the squat, bench press, deadlift, and overhead press.\nBuild dense, athletic muscle mass.\nImprove technical proficiency on competition lifts through increased exposure.\nDevelop work capacity and resilience for long-term progress.\nBalance strength development with physique improvements.\n\nWho It's For\nIntermediate lifters seeking a blend of strength and size.\nPowerlifters wanting more hypertrophy work without sacrificing performance.\nBodybuilders who prioritize progressive strength gains.\nLifters who can consistently train 5 days per week.\nCore Principles\nProgressive Overload: Gradually increasing load, volume, or intensity over time.\nHigh Frequency: Main lifts and movement patterns are trained multiple times weekly.\nStrength First: Heavy compounds form the foundation of every training week.\nHypertrophy Support: Strategic accessory work builds muscle and addresses weak points.\nSustainable Recovery: Volume is distributed across five sessions to manage fatigue.\n\nProgram Motto\n\"Move Heavy. Grow Bigger. Stay Relentless.\"","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":5,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-09-28T16:55:37.174Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Squat and Chest","Shoulder and Arms","Deadlift and Back","Bench prss + overall push","Deadlift + overall pull"],"weeks":[[{"ex